# sources/ is verbatim and append-only -- Ruling 10, sources/README.md rule 1.
#
# Git must never transform anything under it. An end-of-line conversion is
# silent, lossy and invisible on the machine that performs it: the working copy
# keeps the original bytes, so a local verify passes, while the committed blob
# differs and every other checkout fails its manifest hash. That happened on
# 2026-09-24 to the 20 .md files in the export that carried mixed line endings.
#
# -text disables eol conversion in both directions, whatever core.autocrlf is
# set to on the machine doing the commit.
sources/** -text
